[{:seon.task/name "the-branch-roster-is-compacted"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the branch roster is a konserve append log (`datahike.roster`), one entry a `branch!` or delete, never compacted. ``d/branches`` reads the whole log, one konserve read an entry (11.7k ticks and 33 KB each, measured 2026-11-11), deleted branches included: 94k ticks at 1 branch, 1.25 M at 100, 11.8 M and 34 MB at 1,000. A root's store gains a branch an agent, so the log only grows. Correct: the log is folded into one value when it is read past a bound, or a delete rewrites it, so ``d/branches`` costs the live branches (one read when compact). Upstream's own versioning first (`branch-history`, durable GC roots): take its shape if it has one. Proof when built: ``d/branches`` after n branches made and deleted costs what the live ones cost. Absorbed in curation 2026-11-14 (same subject and evidence): seon.db/a-long-running-store-stays-bounded (A user's store runs for months with no one erasing it)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.versioning-test/the-branch-roster-is-compacted}}
 {:seon.task/name "changes-refuses-a-from-off-the-chain-at-once"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by context, 2026-11-16 (message to deps; evidence in seon.ctx/moved-reads-the-commits-between-two-points, landing on jolt/context): ``datahike.versioning/changes`` (versioning.cljc 850-858) walks from `to` by each commit's :base until it meets `from`; when `from` is not on that chain (root's branch after a merge-in, whose commit is built on main) it reads every commit's changes to the log's end before refusing, 59M ticks between two of root's turns [context M result/b8fd550d; the chain read result/d9a27a49]. Cause: the loop's only ends are `from` and nil, so a miss costs the whole lineage. Change: the walk stops at the first commit older than `from` (its graph record's :datahike/generation at or below `from`'s, read once for `from`, or the step's datoms' tx below `from`'s t) and refuses :datahike/changes-not-ancestor there, so a miss costs the commits between them, as a hit does. PRIOR WORK: changes' own loop and its refusals; the commit graph's :datahike/generation (commit-graph-record), read by seon.db/retain!; d/merge-base. COST: estimate O(commits from `to` back to `from`'s generation), one konserve read each, ~12k ticks a read: a miss between two turns ~10 commits ~150k ticks, against 59M today. Proof, red first: datahike.versioning-test/changes-refuses-a-from-off-the-chain-at-once: a branch whose head is built on main after many main commits, asked for changes from a commit off its chain, refuses within reads proportional to the gap, not to main's length."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.versioning-test/changes-refuses-a-from-off-the-chain-at-once}
  :seon.task/estimate #:datahike.versioning{changes {:n 10, :order :linear, :ticks 150000, :bytes 1000000}}}
]
